      "Explanation": "Ācārya is a title or direct form of address for a monastic instructor; in ordination compounds it can designate the office-holder who performs a defined ceremonial role. In encounters the title is often spoken directly to the person being questioned or answered. The bare title does not by itself decide rank, lineage, or ordination office."
